  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "The area of a rectangle is 50 and its perimeter is 30. Find the length of its diagonal.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$5\\sqrt5$ units.\n\nUse $(x+y)^2-2xy=x^2+y^2$ to find the squared diagonal.",
      "worked": "Let the side lengths be $x$ and $y$, and the diagonal be $d$. Then $xy=50$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2y&=30\\\\x+y&=15\\\\(x+y)^2&=225\\\\x^2+2xy+y^2&=225\\\\x^2+y^2&=225-2(50)\\\\x^2+y^2&=125\\\\d&=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}\\\\d&=\\sqrt{125}\\\\d&=5\\sqrt5\\end{align*}$$\nThe diagonal is $5\\sqrt5$ units long.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 92
  },
